{"title":"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>UNIVERSITY OF NORTHERN COLORADO MATHEMATICS CONTEST FINAL ROUND January 28,2006.\n</p><p>For Colorado Students Grades 7-12.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If a dart is thrown at the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcdc43d2ff7165fcb9191f2d81b1e27c9936c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\times 6$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> target, what is the probability that it will hit the shaded area?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df1c252b085c82d7d67511a0e58cc24d9595ae8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw((2,2)--(4,6)--(6,6)--(6,4)--cycle,blue); filldraw((2,2)--(6,2)--(6,1)--cycle,blue); filldraw((2,2)--(0,0)--(0,1)--cycle,blue); filldraw((2,2)--(0,4)--(0,6)--cycle,blue);  for(int i=0;i&lt;7;++i){ draw((0,i)--(6,i),black); draw((i,0)--(i,6),black); } dot((2,2));dot((0,4));dot((0,6));dot((4,6));dot((6,6)); dot((6,4));dot((6,2));dot((6,1));dot((0,0));dot((0,1));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, how many integers are strictly between the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd786cba627222b8d7afe99c09fecbddd145bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)(b+1)(c+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />&#160;? For example, there are 35 integers strictly between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45324826b5d99fc243f7ce05935bb65ed5470486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24=2*3*4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a118fa42c0945f319d25e23fde1794b818c46eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60=3*4*5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first 14 integers are written in order around a circle.\n</p><p>Starting with 1, every fifth integer is underlined. (That is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a354eb67af2769a901159cbc71a2253e7ffced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,6,11,2,7,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />).\nWhat is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400101c6d0547c9231a429d48cc80ed73aae8c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2006^{th}$\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> number underlined?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953b3ed19882010780e63c1f5a6644729f8a74d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(unitcircle,black); pair A; for(int j=1;j&lt;15;++j){ A=dir(90-(j-1)*(360/14)); MP(string(j),A,A); } [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/64792d6ae52edb53227f478f9f562982a9d63237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> divides evenly (without remainder) into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af5ca1c875c0a07ece0afc207dc4768a4f498b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^4-3n^2+10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />&#160;?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e4f2d5cc59e5ffbed3734130e8c45b643adc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the larger triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aed56990dedba5a88a65e21245ccfd5d5e43ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$128$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\nThe area of the trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/9/7c9d11f822493c6fa024726ef0750b2917998e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDEA$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d15d808807bfa561e72dc8111649ed0a204ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Determine the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/e/cee88eb0e94e7831e4d242c8930836c02c7d5128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc13e1d9d8740bc4f6f48868cdc693e5c1b390c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(1,2)--(4,0)--cycle,black); draw((1/2,1)--(2.5,1)--(2,0),black); MP(&quot;A&quot;,(4,0),SE);MP(&quot;C&quot;,(1,2),N);MP(&quot;E&quot;,(0,0),SW); MP(&quot;D&quot;,(.5,1),W);MP(&quot;B&quot;,(2.5,1),NE);MP(&quot;F&quot;,(2,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"148\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of all of the positive integer divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95abd0ed162de8f742f3685bf1a9d857099935a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2=36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e64d1823c10f9befb27fc5c13e02d019e1fedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+6+9+12+18+36=91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"328\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(a) Determine a nice closed formula (i.e. without dots or the summation symbol) for the sum of all positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f156c838ae7d194e36ebf402316e89d42740431a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>(b) Repeat for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4e2cb180f9fd5c9599e2ca4fed24f6d71f6a1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>(c) Generalize.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The five digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c10a61be02be3606a98e013fce75f972145276d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55225$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b1404545adf49090812f9934d4f365c59bdee4c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=e$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58ab3d7140fd1de26a1f70f86718703a2569479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=d$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />; in addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc5d297e083237c0543a09e083ee23f0a199a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55225=235^2=(235)(235)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"209\" height=\"19\" />.\nFind another integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f521656db779d024e6aff0f9a3771ac28d2c3db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> is also a five digit number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/18396b1d04475fed55fd7c1b75cd4d85133210be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcde$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b1404545adf49090812f9934d4f365c59bdee4c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=e$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58ab3d7140fd1de26a1f70f86718703a2569479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=d$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e77a56a52ef16d161f256eb67c49e50855c50b15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3-12n^2+40n-29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"168\" height=\"16\" /> is a prime number. For each of your values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> compute \nthis cubic polynomial showing that it is, in fact, a prime.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine three positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> that simultaneously satisfy the following three conditions:\n</p><p>(i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>(ii) Each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6b7ce92e9ed07d85d84d07822a0cae9593cd95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b,a+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9bbeb7caa1770d1d3cb842655f27e245b08188f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is the square of an integer, and\n</p><p>(iii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is as small as is possible.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many triples of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are there with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d616b4d5fc0192508a07b85cc60baf2377fda9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=401$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the figure below a \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-tableau\" shape. Determine the number of rectangles of all sizes contained within this shape.\nNote that a square is considered a rectangle, and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/4/4c4f94c264467f57f0c7de87e09dd5ee97ee61ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> rectangle is considered different from a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d4e9450e6f37da3ac6d5cacec40ae09d40130a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.\nExpress your answer as a binomial coefficient and explain the significance of your expression. Generalize, with proof, to an \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-tableau\" shape.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/40701260398d42e58abedffd16b69fb89e5e4c30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] for(int j=0;j&lt;5;++j){ draw((0,j)--(min(j+1,4),j),black); draw((j,max(0,j-1))--(j,4),black);  } filldraw((2,2)--(2,3)--(1,3)--(1,2)--cycle,blue); filldraw((2,2)--(3,2)--(3,3)--(2,3)--cycle,blue); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II\">2006 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 UNCO Math Contest II Answer 